<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Interest and depreciation by binomial expansion</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[[[if test="is(g=1)"]]<p>Ksh \({@Pd@}\) is saved in a SACCO account that adds \({@r@}\%\) interest at the end of each year. After \({@n@}\) years the amount is \({@Pd@}(1 + x)^{@n@}\).</p>[[else]]<p>A {@itm@} bought for Ksh \({@Pd@}\) loses \({@r@}\%\) of its value each year. After \({@n@}\) years its value is \({@Pd@}(1 + x)^{@n@}\).</p>[[/if]]<p>(a) What is \(x\)?</p><div>\(x =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) The second term of the expansion of \({@Pd@}(1 + x)^{@n@}\) is \({@Pd@} \times {@n@}x\). Work it out in Ksh.</p><div>Ksh [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>(c) Work out the third term in Ksh.</p><div>Ksh [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div><p>(d) Use the first three terms to estimate the [[if test="is(g=1)"]]amount[[else]]value[[/if]] after \({@n@}\) years, to the nearest shilling.</p><div>Ksh [[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>The first term is the starting amount; the second term, \(P \times nx\), is the [[if test="is(g=1)"]]simple interest[[else]]simple loss[[/if]] over \({@n@}\) years; the later terms are the [[if test="is(g=1)"]]interest earned on interest[[else]]correction for losing a percentage of a smaller value each year[[/if]].</p><p>(a) [[if test="is(g=1)"]]The amount grows by \({@r@}\%\) a year[[else]]The value falls by \({@r@}\%\) a year[[/if]], so \(x = {@xd@}\).</p><p>(b) \({@Pd@} \times {@n@} \times ({@xd@}) = {@T2d@}\)</p><p>(c) The row for power \({@n@}\) starts 1, \({@n@}\), \({@C2@}\), so the third term is \({@Pd@} \times {@C2@} \times ({@xd@})^2 = {@T3d@}\).</p><p>(d) \({@Pd@} + ({@T2d@}) + {@T3d@} = {@E3d@}\), so the estimate is Ksh \({@E3d@}\). The exact value from a calculator is Ksh \({@exd@}\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
